✗ iOS provisioning profile: MISSING — no profile on this machine covers
  com.qanguru.WebDriverAgentRunner.xctrunner for team TEAM7QZ4X2
  Without one, WebDriverAgent cannot be signed, so no run on this machine's
  iPhones can start.
  → run 'nth-agent setup-ios', or open
    ~/.appium/node_modules/appium-xcuitest-driver/node_modules/appium-webdriveragent/WebDriverAgent.xcodeproj
    in Xcode and set your team
  not established: reading a profile off this disk is not running the build: it
  does not establish that Xcode can reach Apple, and it CANNOT say whether the
  developer certificate is trusted on the phone — iOS exposes no such query
  (go-ios v1.3.2 has none, and its misagent profile copy errors), so the first
  session on a phone may still ask you on the device. A development profile also
  LISTS THE DEVICES it covers, and this check reads that list: a udid missing
  from every matching profile fails the build by name before the phone is
  touched.

